{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And they said, Twelve, your servants, are we, brothers, etc.</b> With this they offered a defense against both accusations at once. Regarding that with which he suspected them — 'spies you are' — since they had concealed themselves among the arrivals, they said, 'we are twelve brothers,' and we were afraid of the evil eye. And regarding that with which he suspected them — 'to see the nakedness of the land you have come' — after they had entered through the ten gates of the city, they said, 'and behold, the youngest is with our father today, and one is not,' and on account of the one who is not, we scattered through all ten gates to search for him."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:05.560946260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}